      "summary_short": {
        "zh": "EfficientNet-B3 RA2是timm库的图像分类模型，兼顾算力与精度。其核心是EfficientNet复合缩放法，按比例同步调整深度、宽度与输入分辨率，以强化表示；RA2策略借助RandAugment数据增强，提升训练稳定性与泛化能力。该模型可用于PyTorch迁移学习及特征提取，适合作为实验基线，帮助理解高效网络设计与数据增强的相互作用。",
        "en": "EfficientNet-B3 with the RA2 training recipe is a practical image classification model from the timm library, designed to balance accuracy and computational cost through compound scaling of depth, width, and resolution. It shows how architectural scaling plus strong augmentation…",
        "es": "EfficientNet-B3 with the RA2 training recipe is a practical image classification model from the timm library, designed to balance accuracy and computational cost through compound scaling of depth, width, and resolution. It shows how architectural scaling plus strong augmentation…"
      },
      "summaries": {
        "zh": "EfficientNet-B3 RA2是timm库的图像分类模型，兼顾算力与精度。其核心是EfficientNet复合缩放法，按比例同步调整深度、宽度与输入分辨率，以强化表示；RA2策略借助RandAugment数据增强，提升训练稳定性与泛化能力。该模型可用于PyTorch迁移学习及特征提取，适合作为实验基线，帮助理解高效网络设计与数据增强的相互作用。",
        "en": "EfficientNet-B3 with the RA2 training recipe is a practical image classification model from the timm library, designed to balance accuracy and computational cost through compound scaling of depth, width, and resolution. It shows how architectural scaling plus strong augmentation like RandAugment can yield robust, well-generalizing visual features. You can load this model via timm in PyTorch for transfer learning on custom datasets, extracting embeddings, or as a backbone in vision pipelines. It is a handy baseline for experimenting with efficient model design and training strategies.",
        "es": "EfficientNet-B3 with the RA2 training recipe is a practical image classification model from the timm library, designed to balance accuracy and computational cost through compound scaling of depth, width, and resolution. It shows how architectural scaling plus strong augmentation like RandAugment can yield robust, well-generalizing visual features. You can load this model via timm in PyTorch for transfer learning on custom datasets, extracting embeddings, or as a backbone in vision pipelines. It is a handy baseline for experimenting with efficient model design and training strategies."
      },
